            <div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
                <p n="1">Prosperity! Fortune!</p>
                <p n="1"><gap reason="lost"/> year of the victorious king Nṛpatuṅkavikkiramavarmaṉ.<note>Sanskrit Nṛpatuṅgavikramavarman.</note></p>
                <p n="2"><supplied reason="explanation">the land named</supplied> Kāṟāṇai, <seg cert="low">from</seg> <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>iṭai</foreign></supplied> the Kāṭavati king, the Bhāradvāja <supplied reason="explanation">Brahmin</supplied> who obtained a <foreign>brahmadeya</foreign> <gap reason="lost"/></p>
                <p n="3">two quarters <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>iru-k-kāl-āvatu</foreign></supplied>, to Pūti Tīran alias this Kāṭavati king, this above-<seg cert="low">mentioned</seg> <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>im-mēṟ-co<supplied reason="lost">llapaṭta</supplied></foreign></supplied> <gap reason="lost"/></p>
            </div>
            
            <div type="commentary">
                <p>Incomplete inscription. End of lines covered by later construction (stairs' string wall).</p><!--Update-->
